# SQL review: {{ app_title }}

One SQL file per page of the app, one runnable section per metric, in on-screen
order. Use them to check any number the app shows against the data.

## How to run a section

- **DataGrip** (or another SQL IDE): open this folder, open a page file, put the
  cursor inside a section, and press Cmd/Ctrl+Enter. Each section runs on its
  own; its `params` CTE at the top holds the review window.
- **Snowsight**: paste one section (from its `--N_key` tag to its `;`) into a
  worksheet and run it.
- **Any editor**: the files are plain SQL; read them anywhere.

Each section starts with a tag like `--1_total_revenue`: metric 1 on that page,
key `total_revenue` in `index.yaml`. To change what a section runs, edit
`index.yaml` or the app's `queries/*.sql` and run
`streamsnow sql-review generate {{ app_slug }}`; never edit a page file by hand.
`AGENTS.md` here has the folder rules.

